Package: virtbase-pve-patches
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         patch,
         libpve-storage-perl,
         qemu-server
Description: Virtbase patches for Proxmox VE
 Virtbase needs three changes to Proxmox VE that are not upstream: uploading
 snippets through the storage API, giving an uploaded hookscript its executable
 bit, and accepting the hookscript option on a general VM config update.
 Without them guest provisioning does not work.
 .
 The patched files belong to libpve-storage-perl and qemu-server, so upgrading
 either one reverts the patches. This package carries a dpkg file trigger on
 /usr/share/perl5/PVE and reapplies them whenever anything writes there, which
 is what makes unattended-upgrades safe.
 .
 It also publishes the per-patch state to the node_exporter textfile collector.
 A patch that no longer fits its context after a Proxmox upgrade cannot be
 reapplied by anyone, so that state is alerted on rather than retried.
